Package: com.duoface.carplay.nativescenehost
Name: DuoFace Native Dashboard Scene Host (Development)
Version: 0.1.172~wakefix1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Section: Development
Maintainer: DuoFace Independent
Depends: firmware (>= 16.0), mobilesubstrate
Description: QA172 wakefix1: the QA172 logorecall1 build (QA171 + QA177 H1 controls recall) with the wake path reworked after the 2026-11-04 device A/B proved H1's immediate layoutControls churn clips the hosted keyboard's bottom row. Changes: (1) app-side touch signals now ONLY extend the controls visibility timers in Chrome - they never run a layout pass; a coalesced re-check settles layout after activity stops and stands down while a keyboard is reported up; (2) a transparent first-touch shield window (level 1, above the scene slots, below the controls) covers the panes while the controls are idle, so the first touch wakes the controls DuoNavi-style instead of executing the function under the touch; it arms only when every hosted app can report its keyboard state; (3) the relays report keyboard visibility (UIRemoteKeyboardWindow) on a sibling DF156 mailbox, and the shield never re-arms over a live keyboard. No other change from QA172-QA185 is included. Previous QA171 adds privacy-limited GOFA notification diagnostics to export original notification events and sanitized class/property/key/type metadata only; no traffic payload values, road speed limits, camera alerts or navigation turns are connected or fabricated; preserves persistent on/off and compact handle. Road speed limits/cameras/live route UNVERIFIED; QA162 GOFA-only Speed8 trial (no guessed road limit), plus QA161 scoped first SOLO remote geometry reference 120ms instead of 300ms, preserving media and split safety gates; retains QA160 read-only CarPlay Home trace. Native Home app-grid destination NOT fixed or physically tested. First-party experimental iOS16 rootless CarPlay Native12 integrated candidate with live app cards/recent, logo loading scene, touch activity borders, safer scene resize and foreground-only chrome. Real installed-app picker, source-owned external SBAppViewController host, two visible empty split panes with pass-through input, two clickable controls per pane, scene-ready/failure signals, split/swap/focus/drag and strict disconnect/heartbeat teardown. The CarPlay receiver draws no demo panes or fake action buttons; iPhone shows only actual installed-app inventory and active-session status. No external vendor binary or licensing; actual dual-app rendering and touch on iPhone X/CarPlay not yet device-verified. Opt-in 10-second physical disconnect per-process RunningBoard close with app PID provenance, reconnect cancel and phone foreground guard. Source-verified stage only; CarPlay native map tile/navigation and full iPhone auto-launch or screen-off are not device-verified. Unreleased QA candidate.
